WEBVTT

NOTE target-profiles: written VO text from episode.json, timed from the timeline VO placements

V0-1
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:06.029
Save a full set of station targets
under a name, then switch the

V0-2
00:00:06.129 --> 00:00:09.460
whole course between seasonal and
event strategies in one action.

V1a-1
00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:16.150
Open Settings, then the
Target Profiles tab.

V1b-1
00:00:16.853 --> 00:00:21.301
Profiles sit alongside Calculation and
Minimum Threshold in the settings dialog,

V1b-2
00:00:21.401 --> 00:00:25.183
because a profile is a calculation
input rather than a station edit.

V2a-1
00:00:31.436 --> 00:00:36.625
The tab lists five profile slots for
each Lynx course, with Last Updated,

V2a-2
00:00:36.725 --> 00:00:40.706
Stations, Update from Current
and Apply Profile columns.

V2b-1
00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:44.514
Each profile shows when
it was last updated,

V2b-2
00:00:44.614 --> 00:00:49.376
by renaming it or with Update from
Current, and how many stations it holds.

V2b-3
00:00:49.476 --> 00:00:53.350
An empty slot shows two dashes
for Last Updated and Stations.

V3a-1
00:00:59.253 --> 00:01:03.903
Applying overwrites the Target VWC
of every station the profile covers.

V3a-2
00:01:04.003 --> 00:01:06.491
Because that is a recalculation input,

V3a-3
00:01:06.591 --> 00:01:11.373
the dashboard reloads and the Suggested
column changes across the course.

V3b-1
00:01:12.336 --> 00:01:14.919
Applying a profile is
a course-wide change.

V3b-2
00:01:15.019 --> 00:01:19.286
Applying and pushing in the same
minute leaves no time to sanity-check.

V4a-1
00:01:27.193 --> 00:01:31.316
Once the course is tuned the way you
want it, save the state as a profile

V4a-2
00:01:31.416 --> 00:01:35.482
so you can return to it. Name it for
the condition rather than the date,

V4a-3
00:01:35.582 --> 00:01:39.593
the reason you set those targets is
what you will be looking for later.

V4b-1
00:01:40.593 --> 00:01:44.753
The station targets currently in the table
are what a new profile would capture.
